      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Look, Candidate A is technically sharp, but when she spoke, I just felt like she lacked that polished executive presence; maybe she won't gel with the leadership team.\" Or, in reference to Candidate B, \"She's brilliant on paper, sure, but her delivery felt a bit hesitant; I'm worried about how she'll handle the high-pressure client meetings.\" These small hesitations reveal the subconscious prioritization of vocal presentation over demonstrated capability. The dialogue showcases how subtle language undermines objective evaluation.",
